               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=a4caa9fe-de1e-49c5-92de-50ed9c22a42d",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Terrain\n\nIn every addition, squares represent the digits. When a column carries 1, the result can go beyond the 10 possible values (the digits from 0 to 9), and extra squares appear outside the group of ten. So, before you start adding two digits, ask yourself: is the second digit greater or smaller than the complement of the first? That answer tells you whether the column will carry 1.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "fa0f472b-0543-4b85-98db-79f42dfd0730",
